## Why does the count on a step not go to zero?

The count includes items on hold and items posted to suspense: they are set aside, not finished. Items waiting for the client are not counted as needing action, but they are counted by the quarter check "Nothing is waiting for the client". Open the step and use the **Needs action** or **On hold** filter to find the remaining items.

## Why must reading be approved?

Documents with a text layer (PDF, Excel, CSV, Word) are read at no cost. Scanned PDFs and photos are read by an AI model, which has a cost. Operon shows the price first, and a scanned file is read only after approval. A file that is not approved is not booked.

## Does switching the interface language change the AI employee's language?

No. The **EN | 中** switch changes only the language of the interface. The AI employee replies in the language of the question it is asked.

## The client has sent a missing document. Where does it go?

Record it as the answer on the client query list, with the document attached (see [Ask the client](/en/bookkeeping/client-queries/)). A missing bank statement is uploaded with **Import documents** in step 1 instead.

## Can a completed quarter be changed?

Only after a manager reopens it. See [Reopen a period](/en/bookkeeping/reopen/).
